% The Ponens policies ponens-defaults, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 39
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 8 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 50.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* in its chain; known as chain_link.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* on its target; known as target_link.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    item *an item* of *a collection* has *a value* as *a field*; known as item_field.
    artifact *an artifact* is made by step *a step*; known as made_by_event.
    step *a step* uses artifact *an artifact*; known as uses_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind_event.
    artifact *an artifact* derives from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derives_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a verification goal for artifact *an other artifact*; known as goal_target_event.
    file *a file* is edited; known as edited_event.
    file *a file* is declared as modified; known as declared_event.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* is in the chain of step *an other step*; known as in_chain.
    step *a step* shares a target with step *an other step*; known as shares_target.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    item *an item* of *a collection* had *a value* as *a field*; known as item_had.
    artifact *an artifact* was made by step *a step*; known as made_by.
    step *a step* used artifact *an artifact*; known as used.
    artifact *an artifact* was a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind.
    artifact *an artifact* derived from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derived.
    artifact *an artifact* was a verification goal for artifact *an other artifact*; known as goal_target.
    file *a file* was edited; known as edited.
    file *a file* was declared as modified; known as declared.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    step *a step* meets *a condition* with step *an other step*; known as meets_with.
    the trace meets *a condition*; known as trace_meets.
    artifact *an artifact* meets *a condition*; known as artifact_meets.
    artifact *an artifact* meets *a condition* with step *a step*; known as artifact_meets_step.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.
    the policy *a policy* is broken; known as broken.

the knowledge base ponens defaults includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step comes after step an other step in its chain
then step the other step is in the chain of step the step.

when step a step comes after step an other step on its target
then step the other step shares a target with step the step.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

when item an item of a collection has a value as a field
then item the item of the collection had the value as the field.

when artifact an artifact is made by step a step
then artifact the artifact was made by step the step.

when step a step uses artifact an artifact
then step the step used artifact the artifact.

when artifact an artifact is a a kind artifact
then artifact the artifact was a the kind artifact.

when artifact an artifact derives from artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact derived from artifact the other artifact.

when artifact an artifact is a verification goal for artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact was a verification goal for artifact the other artifact.

when file a file is edited
then file the file was edited.

when file a file is declared as modified
then file the file was declared as modified.


% accessibility_state_managed (warning): G(EditFile ∧ aria_state_component → P_chain(Verify ∧ a11y_state_correct))
% Incorrect ARIA state causes accessibility tools to report wrong information. A dropdown that sets aria-expanded=true but never sets it back to false on close is broken for screen reader users.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows a11y state correct" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "a11y state correct" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and step the step has shown "aria state component"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows a11y state correct"
then the policy accessibility_state_managed is broken at step the step.

% all_actions_have_rationale (error): G(action → rationale ≠ ∅)
% Ensures every step is explainable. Critical for audit trails and debugging agent behavior.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "action"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "rationale ≠ ∅"
then the policy all_actions_have_rationale is broken at step the step.

% all_decisions_justified (error): G(gateway → rationale ≠ ∅)
% Decision points are where the agent chose between alternatives. The reasoning must be recorded for review.
when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "gateway"
    and it is not the case that step the step has shown "rationale ≠ ∅"
then the policy all_decisions_justified is broken at step the step.

% animation_state_deterministic (info): G(Formalize ∧ animation_state → F(Verify ∧ deterministic))
% Non-deterministic animations cause visual glitches: elements stuck mid-transition, competing animations, or states that depend on timing. Verifying determinism ensures consistent UX.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows deterministic" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "deterministic" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "animation state"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows deterministic"
then the policy animation_state_deterministic is broken at step the step.

% api_breaking_change_flagged (error): G(EditFile ∧ api_endpoint → P_chain(Verify ∧ (proved ∧ backward_compatible) ∨ (refuted ∧ P UserApproval)))
% Unintentional API breaking changes cause downstream failures. Formal verification of the API contract catches field removals, type changes, and semantic shifts.
step a step meets "is a Verify and shows proved and shows backward compatible or shows refuted and an earlier step is a UserApproval" at a time if
    step the step was a Verify at the time
    and step the step has shown "proved" at the time
    and step the step has shown "backward compatible" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time.

step a step meets "is a Verify and shows proved and shows backward compatible or shows refuted and an earlier step is a UserApproval" at a time if
    step the step has shown "refuted" at the time
    and step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and shows backward compatible or shows refuted and an earlier step is a UserApproval" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step meets "is a Verify and shows proved and shows backward compatible or shows refuted and an earlier step is a UserApproval" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and step the step has shown "api endpoint"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and shows backward compatible or shows refuted and an earlier step is a UserApproval"
then the policy api_breaking_change_flagged is broken at step the step.

% approval_before_deploy (error): G(Deploy → P UserApproval)
% Automated deployments by AI agents should always have a human gate.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Deploy
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval"
then the policy approval_before_deploy is broken at step the step.

% assumptions_are_located (warning): ∀ r ∈ residuals . r.kind = Assumption → (r.target ≠ ∅ ∨ r.related_artifact_ids ≠ ∅)
% An assumption the work relies on is only reviewable if a reviewer can find what it touches. An unlocated assumption ('I assumed something somewhere') gives the reviewer nowhere to point. Requiring a target or related artifacts keeps the residual surface navigable.
when the session ends
    and item a residual of residuals had "assumption" as kind
    and it is not the case that item the residual of residuals had "yes" as located
then the policy assumptions_are_located is broken.

% async_state_transitions_verified (error): G(Formalize ∧ async_state_machine → F(Verify ∧ (proved ∨ sat)))
% Async state machines (idle → loading → success/error) are deceptively simple but have subtle issues: race conditions, stale responses, retry logic. Formal verification ensures all paths terminate correctly.
step a step meets "shows proved or shows sat" at a time if
    step the step has shown "proved" at the time.

step a step meets "shows proved or shows sat" at a time if
    step the step has shown "sat" at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved or shows sat" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step meets "shows proved or shows sat" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "async state machine"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved or shows sat"
then the policy async_state_transitions_verified is broken at step the step.

% data_flow_integrity (error): G(∀input ∈ inputs(a) → ∃!b . b < a ∧ input ∈ outputs(b))
% Ensures the artifact dependency graph is well-formed. Broken data flow means an action used data that was never produced.
artifact an artifact meets "made before" with step a step at a time if
    artifact the artifact was made by step an other step at the time
    and the other step < the step.

step a step meets "uses an artifact made at or after it, or by no step" at a time if
    step the step used artifact an artifact at the time
    and it is not the case that artifact the artifact meets "made before" with step the step at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step meets "uses an artifact made at or after it, or by no step"
then the policy data_flow_integrity is broken.

% database_migration_verified (error): G(RunCommand ∧ db_migration → P_chain(Verify ∧ proved ∧ migration_safe))
% Irreversible migrations that lose data are catastrophic. Formalizing the migration as a state transition and verifying reversibility catches destructive operations before they run.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and shows migration safe" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "proved" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "migration safe" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a RunCommand
    and step the step has shown "db migration"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and shows migration safe"
then the policy database_migration_verified is broken at step the step.

% destructive_actions_confirmed (error): G(DeleteFile → P_chain UserApproval)
% Prevents accidental data loss. Uses P_chain to ensure the approval is contextually related to the delete, not just a coincidental earlier approval.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a UserApproval" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a DeleteFile
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a UserApproval"
then the policy destructive_actions_confirmed is broken at step the step.

% explain_before_complex_change (info): G(complex_change → P(Explain ∨ ReportProgress))
% Users should understand what the agent is about to do before large-scale changes.
step a step meets "is a Explain or is a ReportProgress" at a time if
    step the step was a Explain at the time.

step a step meets "is a Explain or is a ReportProgress" at a time if
    step the step was a ReportProgress at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a Explain or is a ReportProgress" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step meets "is a Explain or is a ReportProgress" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step has shown "complex change"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a Explain or is a ReportProgress"
then the policy explain_before_complex_change is broken at step the step.

% files_modified_consistent (warning): files_modified = {target(a) | G(a ∧ (EditFile ∨ CreateFile ∨ DeleteFile))}
% Catches discrepancies between declared and actual file changes. Important for accurate commit messages and change tracking.
when the session ends
    and file a file was edited
    and it is not the case that file the file was declared as modified
then the policy files_modified_consistent is broken.

when the session ends
    and file a file was declared as modified
    and it is not the case that file the file was edited
then the policy files_modified_consistent is broken.

% form_validation_complete (warning): G(Formalize ∧ form_validation → F(Decompose ∧ complete))
% Form validation often has edge cases: empty strings, whitespace-only, unicode, boundary values. Decomposition finds every distinct validation path and generates test cases for each.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows complete" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Decompose at the time
    and step the second step has shown "complete" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "form validation"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows complete"
then the policy form_validation_complete is broken at step the step.

% goals_reference_valid_artifacts (error): G(VerificationGoal → target_artifact_id ∈ {a.id | a.type = IMLModel})
% A verification goal without a valid model reference is meaningless — there's nothing to verify against.
when the session ends
    and artifact an artifact was a verification goal for artifact an other artifact
    and it is not the case that artifact the other artifact was a IMLModel artifact
then the policy goals_reference_valid_artifacts is broken.

% high_severity_residuals_acknowledged_before_commit (error): G(GitCommit → ∀ r ∈ residuals . r.severity ≥ High → r.status ≠ Open)
% Commits are where work crosses a boundary into the shared history. Requiring high-severity residuals to be explicitly acknowledged before commit ensures a reviewer downstream inherits a triaged residual surface, not a pile of silent open gaps.
when the session ends
    and the trace has shown "a commit"
    and item a residual of residuals had "critical" as severity
    and item the residual of residuals had "open" as status
then the policy high_severity_residuals_acknowledged_before_commit is broken.

when the session ends
    and the trace has shown "a commit"
    and item a residual of residuals had "high" as severity
    and item the residual of residuals had "open" as status
then the policy high_severity_residuals_acknowledged_before_commit is broken.

% lint_before_commit (warning): G(GitCommit → P(Lint ∧ completed))
% Catches formatting issues, unused imports, and common bugs before they enter the codebase.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a Lint and shows completed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a Lint at the time
    and step the second step has shown "completed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a Lint and shows completed"
then the policy lint_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% no_force_push (error): G(¬(GitPush ∧ force))
% Force pushing destroys commit history for other collaborators. This is almost never the right action for an AI agent.
when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitPush
    and step the step has shown "force"
then the policy no_force_push is broken at step the step.

% no_open_critical_residuals (error): ¬∃ r ∈ residuals . r.severity = Critical ∧ r.status = Open
% The residual surface is the trace's declared negative space. Approving a change while it still carries an open critical gap defeats the purpose of declaring it. This makes 'gaps declared, located, and triaged' enforceable at the most consequential level.
when the session ends
    and item a residual of residuals had "critical" as severity
    and item the residual of residuals had "open" as status
then the policy no_open_critical_residuals is broken.

% no_secrets_committed (error): G(GitCommit → ¬P(CreateFile ∧ secret_pattern))
% Accidentally committing secrets is a common and severe security vulnerability.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a CreateFile and shows secret pattern" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a CreateFile at the time
    and step the second step has shown "secret pattern" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and step the step meets "an earlier step is a CreateFile and shows secret pattern"
then the policy no_secrets_committed is broken at step the step.

% pci_compliance_review (error): G(EditFile ∧ pci_scope → P_chain(VerificationResult(proved) ∧ pci_constraints))
% PCI DSS violations carry severe penalties. Formal verification against PCI constraints catches issues like accidental logging of card numbers that code review often misses.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows pci constraints" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step has shown "VerificationResult(proved)" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "pci constraints" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and step the step has shown "pci scope"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows pci constraints"
then the policy pci_compliance_review is broken at step the step.

% plaid_token_lifecycle_conformance (error): G(Formalize ∧ plaid_domain → P_chain(VerificationResult(proved) ∧ ref_model(ref_plaid_link)))
% Plaid's Link token lifecycle has strict ordering requirements. Exchanging a token before the user completes Link, or using an expired token, causes silent failures that are hard to debug.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows ref_model(ref_plaid_link)" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step has shown "VerificationResult(proved)" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "ref_model(ref_plaid_link)" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "plaid domain"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows ref_model(ref_plaid_link)"
then the policy plaid_token_lifecycle_conformance is broken at step the step.

% react_effect_cleanup_verified (warning): G(EditFile ∧ react_effect_with_subscription → P_chain(Verify ∧ cleanup_correct))
% Missing or incorrect cleanup in useEffect is a common source of memory leaks and stale state bugs in React applications. Formalizing the setup/teardown contract and verifying it catches issues that are hard to reproduce manually.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows cleanup correct" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "cleanup correct" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and step the step has shown "react effect with subscription"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows cleanup correct"
then the policy react_effect_cleanup_verified is broken at step the step.

% reducer_action_coverage (warning): G(Formalize ∧ reducer → F(Decompose ∧ all_actions_handled))
% Reducers with missing action handlers silently return the previous state, which can cause subtle bugs. Decomposition reveals every action × state combination and whether the result is well-defined.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows all actions handled" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Decompose at the time
    and step the second step has shown "all actions handled" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "reducer"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows all actions handled"
then the policy reducer_action_coverage is broken at step the step.

% regulated_change_audit_trail (error): G(GitCommit ∧ regulated_scope → P_chain(ReadFile) ∧ P_chain(Verify ∧ proved) ∧ P(UserApproval) ∧ P(RunTests ∧ completed))
% SOX, HIPAA, and financial regulations require demonstrable evidence that changes were reviewed, tested, and approved. This policy makes the audit trail machine-checkable.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a ReadFile" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a ReadFile at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "proved" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval (2)" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a UserApproval at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a RunTests at the time
    and step the second step has shown "completed" at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a ReadFile and an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and an earlier step is a UserApproval and an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed" at a time if
    step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a ReadFile" at the time
    and step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved" at the time
    and step the step meets "an earlier step is a UserApproval (2)" at the time
    and step the step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and step the step has shown "regulated scope"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a ReadFile and an earlier step in its chain is a Verify and shows proved and an earlier step is a UserApproval and an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed"
then the policy regulated_change_audit_trail is broken at step the step.

% research_before_edit (warning): G(EditFile → P_target(ReadFile ∨ ReadDocumentation ∨ SearchCode ∨ AnalyzeCode))
% Prevents blind edits. The agent should understand the code before modifying it. Uses P_target to ensure the research is about the same file being edited.
step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation" at a time if
    step the step was a ReadFile at the time.

step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation" at a time if
    step the step was a ReadDocumentation at the time.

step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation" at the time.

step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode" at a time if
    step the step was a SearchCode at the time.

step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode or is a AnalyzeCode" at a time if
    step the step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode" at the time.

step a step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode or is a AnalyzeCode" at a time if
    step the step was a AnalyzeCode at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step on its target is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode or is a AnalyzeCode" at a time if
    step a second step shares a target with step the step at the time
    and step the second step meets "is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode or is a AnalyzeCode" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step on its target is a ReadFile or is a ReadDocumentation or is a SearchCode or is a AnalyzeCode"
then the policy research_before_edit is broken at step the step.

% route_guard_complete (error): G(Formalize ∧ route_guard → F(Decompose ∧ complete))
% Missing route guards expose protected pages to unauthorized users. Decomposition ensures every route is checked against every possible auth state: logged out, logged in (no role), admin, expired token, etc.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows complete (2)" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Decompose at the time
    and step the second step has shown "complete" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "route guard"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows complete (2)"
then the policy route_guard_complete is broken at step the step.

% stripe_conformance_required (error): G(Formalize ∧ stripe_domain → P_chain(VerificationResult(proved) ∧ ref_model(ref_stripe_payments)))
% Payment processing code must conform to the canonical Stripe API state machine. The agent's formalization must be proved to be a valid refinement of the reference model.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows ref_model(ref_stripe_payments)" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step has shown "VerificationResult(proved)" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "ref_model(ref_stripe_payments)" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "stripe domain"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain shows VerificationResult(proved) and shows ref_model(ref_stripe_payments)"
then the policy stripe_conformance_required is broken at step the step.

% tests_before_commit (error): G(GitCommit → P(RunTests ∧ completed))
% Prevents untested code from entering the repository. A fundamental CI/CD gate.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed (2)" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a RunTests at the time
    and step the second step has shown "completed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed (2)"
then the policy tests_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% tests_pass_before_commit (error): G(GitCommit → (RunTests ∧ completed) S_last GitCommit)
% Stronger than tests_before_commit: ensures the most recent test state is clean, not just that some test ran at some point.
step a step meets "a step from it to the other step is a GitCommit" with step an other step at a time if
    step a third step has ended at the time
    and the third step >= the step
    and the third step < the other step
    and step the third step was a GitCommit at the time.

step a step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed since the last step that is a GitCommit" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a RunTests at the time
    and step the second step has shown "completed" at the time
    and it is not the case that step the second step meets "a step from it to the other step is a GitCommit" with step the step at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a RunTests and shows completed since the last step that is a GitCommit"
then the policy tests_pass_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% trace_has_proper_lifecycle (error): start_event ∧ F end_event
% A well-formed trace must have clear boundaries. Incomplete traces indicate crashes or abandoned sessions.
the trace meets "some step the trace has ended" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and the trace has shown "end event" at the time.

the trace meets "the trace: the trace has started and it or a later step the trace has ended" at a time if
    the trace has shown "start event" at the time
    and the trace meets "some step the trace has ended" at the time.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "the trace: the trace has started and it or a later step the trace has ended"
then the policy trace_has_proper_lifecycle is broken.

% two_person_approval_for_infra (error): G(EditFile ∧ infra_scope → P(UserApproval ∧ approver_1) ∧ P(UserApproval ∧ approver_2 ∧ approver_2 ≠ approver_1))
% Single-person approval for infrastructure is a common audit finding. Two-person approval prevents both accidental and malicious infrastructure changes.
% Ponens cannot evaluate this formula ("too complex for runtime evaluation"): no law.

% type_check_before_commit (warning): G(GitCommit → P(TypeCheck ∧ completed))
% Type errors caught early prevent runtime failures.
step a step meets "an earlier step is a TypeCheck and shows completed" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step < the step
    and step the second step was a TypeCheck at the time
    and step the second step has shown "completed" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a GitCommit
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step is a TypeCheck and shows completed"
then the policy type_check_before_commit is broken at step the step.

% ui_state_machine_decomposed (warning): G(Formalize ∧ ui_state_machine ∧ complex → F(Decompose))
% Manual testing of state machines is error-prone because the number of paths grows exponentially. Region decomposition by ImandraX finds every distinct execution path and generates a test for each.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Decompose at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "ui state machine"
    and step the step has shown "complex"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose"
then the policy ui_state_machine_decomposed is broken at step the step.

% unverified_residuals_have_suggested_check (warning): ∀ r ∈ residuals . r.kind = Unverified → r.suggested_check ≠ ∅
% An unverified claim is only actionable to a reviewer if it says how it could be verified. Requiring a suggested_check turns the negative space from a warning into a work-list, and is what makes the agent-to-agent handoff productive rather than merely cautionary.
when the session ends
    and item a residual of residuals had "unverified" as kind
    and it is not the case that item the residual of residuals had "given" as suggested_check
then the policy unverified_residuals_have_suggested_check is broken.

% xstate_deadlock_free (error): G(Formalize ∧ xstate_domain → F(Verify ∧ proved ∧ deadlock_free))
% A deadlocked state machine leaves the UI stuck with no way forward. This is especially critical for multi-step flows (checkout, onboarding, wizards) where users cannot recover without a page refresh.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved and shows deadlock free" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "proved" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "deadlock free" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "xstate domain"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved and shows deadlock free"
then the policy xstate_deadlock_free is broken at step the step.

% xstate_guards_verified (error): G(Formalize ∧ xstate_guards → F(Verify ∧ proved ∧ guard_completeness))
% XState guards determine which transitions fire. If guards have gaps (events that match no guard) or overlaps (events that match multiple guards), the machine has undefined behavior. Formal verification catches this exhaustively.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved and shows guard completeness" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Verify at the time
    and step the second step has shown "proved" at the time
    and step the second step has shown "guard completeness" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "xstate guards"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Verify and shows proved and shows guard completeness"
then the policy xstate_guards_verified is broken at step the step.

% xstate_machine_formalized (error): G(EditFile ∧ xstate_machine → P_chain(Formalize ∧ xstate_domain))
% XState machines define critical application logic. Formalizing them into IML enables exhaustive verification of all state transitions, guard conditions, and event handling — something unit tests alone cannot guarantee.
step a step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Formalize and shows xstate domain" at a time if
    step a second step is in the chain of step the step at the time
    and step the second step was a Formalize at the time
    and step the second step has shown "xstate domain" at the time.

when step a step ends
    and step the step was a EditFile
    and step the step has shown "xstate machine"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "an earlier step in its chain is a Formalize and shows xstate domain"
then the policy xstate_machine_formalized is broken at step the step.

% xstate_reachability_checked (warning): G(Formalize ∧ xstate_domain → F(Decompose ∧ all_states_reachable))
% Unreachable states waste code and confuse developers. Region decomposition reveals which states are actually reachable and what conditions lead to them.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows all states reachable" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a Decompose at the time
    and step the second step has shown "all states reachable" at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Formalize
    and step the step has shown "xstate domain"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a Decompose and shows all states reachable"
then the policy xstate_reachability_checked is broken at step the step.

